  "title": "Storage: secure persistence",
  "notes": "2026-08-27 secure-persistence aggregate audit after Zephyr identity-store completion: NOT COMPLETE and no source edits made in this leaf. Proven satisfied slices: Zephyr app identity now has bounded versioned EUI/public-key/CRC records, record-before-marker commit/recovery, fail-closed corruption/error semantics and deterministic qemu_x86 reboot tests (l1qw.11.2.1, IPv6 off/on 15/15); Zephyr TOFU has an authenticated two-generation Settings backend and deterministic torn/corrupt/rollback tests (l1qw.6.6.2.8); Python transactional OSCORE SQLite context persistence is closed (2auf.66); Zephyr OSCORE sender persistence mechanics and NVM failure paths exist.\\n\\nRead-only production wiring audit found unresolved guarantees: (1) identity CRC/marker has no independent authenticated monotonic/deletion rollback authority; (2) lichen_key_store_settings_init has no production caller, auth-key source, or durable trusted min_revision provider; (3) lichen_l2_init unconditionally clears RAM-only link replay windows on reboot; (4) oscore_nvm_register_callbacks has no production caller and recipient replay windows are RAM-only. Created exact P1 blockers hcbi, s2qx, szi7, and 4num and linked them.\\n\\nAlso linked active owned blockers instead of colliding: Python identity rollback rxer; Rust gateway identity atomic create/error/permissions/first-boot xyk3,2502,izg5,so3l; trust authentication/durability 68st,ffnz,ywv6,ta0c; Link restart/rollback/transaction/concurrency/import c1fr,62e4,m1az,szxc,uf09; OSCORE rollback/sender/recipient 5rx2,h8ol,mamj. Both sibling agents confirmed no current persistence-path overlap, but these Beads are already in_progress under external ownership. The immediately preceding same-tree deterministic qemu_x86 app_identity Settings/core gates remain green (IPv6 off/on 15/15); no rerun was necessary because this aggregate made no source changes.",
